# Build context for the registry image.
#
# The context is ALLOWLISTED: `**` excludes everything, and then each
# thing the image needs is re-included. That is deliberate — the
# repository root is 1.1 GB of game assets, and an image that carries
# them is slow to build and leaks content.
#
# The registry's modules are re-included as a DIRECTORY, not one line
# per file. With one line per file, adding a module meant remembering
# to add a line HERE as well as to the Dockerfile, and forgetting
# either one ships an image that cannot start:
#
#   - the Dockerfile copies it but the allowlist does not → the build
#     fails with a checksum error (the leaderboard's modules, commit
#     514934a; the log-state module, later the same day);
#   - neither list mentions it → the build succeeds, the image is
#     missing the module, and the registry crash-loops in production
#     with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND (console-ask.mjs, 2026-10-28).
#
# One directory re-include means a new module is in the image because
# it exists, not because somebody remembered.
**
!services/registry/Dockerfile.registry
!services/registry/package.json
!services/registry/service.mjs
!services/registry/lib/
!webxash/vite-a2s-plugin.mjs
